WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:04.558
This is the executive briefing
for Identity and Directory,

3
00:00:04.558 --> 00:00:09.284
one of the books of the Federal
Modernization Workbook, for the people who

4
00:00:09.284 --> 00:00:14.087
make the calls: the CIO, the CISO, the
identity program lead and the sponsors.

5
00:00:14.087 --> 00:00:15.513
The argument is short.

6
00:00:15.513 --> 00:00:18.992
Zero Trust moved the access
decision onto identity,

7
00:00:18.992 --> 00:00:23.362
so whatever the directory believes,
every application enforces.

8
00:00:23.362 --> 00:00:25.821
And syncing the forest as it stands just

9
00:00:25.821 --> 00:00:28.725
copies twenty-five years
of risk into the cloud.

10
00:00:28.725 --> 00:00:32.840
What this book accomplishes is a
directory where placement has become

11
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.025
attributes and rules, and every service
account has an owner and a target.

12
00:00:37.025 --> 00:00:41.731
It carries the directory side of the
HR track and the service accounts;

13
00:00:41.731 --> 00:00:46.194
people's attributes are in HR-Driven
Identity, devices and servers

14
00:00:46.194 --> 00:00:50.575
in Devices and Endpoints, and AI
agents in AI Identity Governance.

15
00:00:50.575 --> 00:00:53.330
Let's start with where
access gets decided now.
